# heap.bot -- the C-pointer half of the tagged-pointer reproducer
# (RN-ANDROID-TAGGED-POINTER-CORRECTNESS-MILESTONE-1.md, "The original
# defect"): a heap block C allocates, kept and handed back, and no byte
# exposure at all -- so that the pointer result's refusal (NATIVE ADDRESS,
# SDL_CreateWindow's in the earlier milestone) is seen apart from the byte
# exposure's (hello.bot's CORE SEMANTIC RANGE). Where Bionic tags heap
# pointers, a runtime whose C address word cannot hold the tag refuses
# tp_alloc's result; one that can hands it back unchanged.
import std::ffi::c
import tp

p = tp::alloc(64)
q = std::ffi::c::clone(p)
same = p.same()
q.release()
same
